        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Indus Valley Civilisation</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The plains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> and of the seasonal Ghaggar-Hakra river and their borderlands, in most of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> and north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, with an outpost at Shortughai in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 3300–1300 BCE: the Early Harappan phase from c. 3300 BCE, the mature urban phase c. 2600–1900 BCE, then the Late Harappan phase of villages until c. 1300 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Planned cities of baked brick with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and covered drains; the Great Bath of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohenjo-daro">Mohenjo-daro</a>; carved stamp seals with an undeciphered script; standard weights; trade by sea with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Excavations since the 1920s at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harappa">Harappa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohenjo-daro">Mohenjo-daro</a>, Kalibangan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothal">Lothal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dholavira">Dholavira</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakhigarhi">Rakhigarhi</a> and many smaller sites; some 4,000 to 5,000 short inscriptions, still unread; Mesopotamian texts on the trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meluhha">Meluhha</a></span></div>
        </div>
